I am covering the grid cell where there is one JSON object located both inside a code fence and outside a code fence (meaning the same object is repeated), with prose appearing between the two objects. According to the rules for `conformance.kernel.recovery`, the harness recovers the last object inside a code fence when any fence holds one, and if no fence holds one, it takes the last top-level object. In this case, the object in the fence is the priority. Moving the prose from between the objects to before the first object does not change the fact that there is an object in a fence, nor does it change which object is the last one in a fence, so the recovered object should remain unchanged.